<article class="env-definition" id="00Z2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00Z2">Definition <span data-tag="00Z2">7.47.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $f : V \to U$ be a morphism of $\mathcal{C}$. Let $S \subset h_ U$ be a sieve. We define the <em>pullback of $S$ by $f$</em> to be the sieve $S \times _ U V$ of $V$ defined by the rule </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\alpha : T \to V) \in (S \times _ U V)(T) \Leftrightarrow (f \circ \alpha : T \to U) \in S(T)  \]
</div>
</article>